# Review and merge in four lanes (434-context, 06 Standards/434_Contributor_Standard.md §10).
#
# This file is the lane map. A path owned by @434media/founder is lane 1 (rule changes)
# or lane 2 (sensitive code): the founder approves it. A path listed below with no owner
# is lane 3 (code people see): the founder sees a preview, the review agent and the
# checks approve. Anything not matched is lane 4: it merges once the checks pass.
# A change that touches more than one lane takes the strictest.
#
# Inert until the rulesets exist. Today it requires nothing: GitHub only asks a code owner
# to review, and the team @434media/founder does not exist yet, so GitHub reports this file
# as having an unknown owner until the setup creates it. The setup is
# 434-context `04 Build/434_Four_Lane_Setup.md`.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so lane 3 comes first and the owned lanes override it.
# CODEOWNERS has no [ ] ranges, so Next.js segments like [id] are matched with *.

